  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Each page is a black and white drawing composed of periods and connecting lines. The periods were marked from each page of the artist's copy of Ernest Hemingway's "The old man and the sea."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"I began by cutting down semi-transparent mylar sheets to mirror the pages of my book .... After marking each period, I drew lines between the points to track the flow of these tiny pauses in the novel. Each constellation of periods reflects both the book's passages of long descriptive passages as well as its fleeting moments of dialog.--Artists' statement, page [129].</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Condition: no library markings, in protective enclosure.</subfield>
